# Semgrep ignore list — paths excluded from SAST scanning.
# CI: see .github/workflows/ci.yml (semgrep job).
#
# Rationale: third-party code and build artifacts are out of scope for our SAST
# review; scanning them adds noise and false positives. Semgrep's own defaults
# already skip .git/, node_modules/; we add project-specific exclusions below.

# Build output (all crates' compiled artifacts + the workspace target dir).
target/
**/target/

# The fuzz crate uses libfuzzer-sys FFI (inherently unsafe by design) and does
# not inherit workspace lints. Its quality is enforced separately.
fuzz/

# Playwright e2e suite is TypeScript, out of the Rust SAST scope (gitleaks covers
# secret scanning there).
e2e/node_modules/
e2e/

# Generated GitHub Pages site assets (static HTML/CSS) — not audited Rust.
docs/

# Lockfiles are machine-generated; scanning them produces deterministic noise.
Cargo.lock
**/package-lock.json
**/yarn.lock

# Supply-chain config (TOML with rule URLs that trip generic rules).
supply-chain/
